Wilhelm — short, focused session today to build consistency and confidence with the bow.

Plan (60 minutes)
- Safety & equipment check (5 min): inspect bow, arrows, string, rest; set a safe target—never an apple on a person.
- Warm-up (10 min): light shoulder/rotator cuff mobility, 20 low-tension draws to groove form.
- Fundamentals drill (20 min): 3 sets of 10 shots at 10 m concentrating on stance, relaxed grip, identical anchor point, steady bow arm, smooth release, and full follow-through. After each set, note one thing to correct.
- Grouping drill (15 min): aim for tight group — 5 arrows trying to land within a 10 cm circle; repeat 4 times. If groups scatter, slow down the shot process and breathe.
- Cool-down & reflection (10 min): jot what improved, what to fix next session; 5 minutes visualization of a perfect shot.

Specific cue to use: "Stance — anchor — breath — release — hold." Breathe out gently on release.

Today's measurable goal: consistent anchor and a 5-arrow group inside 10 cm at 10 m.

Motivating claim: Do this today and your consistency will leap forward — keep at it and that apple will tremble, Wilhelm Tell.
